# Keep the build context small and the image reproducible. The host .venv
# is the single most important exclusion: it is built against the host's
# interpreter (here python3.14) and would silently shadow the image's own
# uv-managed 3.12 venv if copied in. Everything else here is either
# regenerated in-image, host-only, or runtime cruft.
# Ref: https://docs.docker.com/build/building/context/#dockerignore-files
.venv/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.traj.json
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.claude/
htmlcov/
.coverage
